{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 128, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip on edge 3 gave +6/+5.8/+20 when edge 0 was none (run 11), versus about +1 to +5 and +2 to +16 with any other edge 0 op, since the skip then supplies the missing input-to-output path."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Upgrading edge 2 gave about 0 gain when edge 1 was already a 3x3 conv (run 4) but +2 to +7 with other edge 1 ops (runs 1-3, 5), so the two edges' gains overlap."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Upgrading edge 0 gave only about +1/0/+0.8 when edge 3 was already a 3x3 conv (run 9), versus +2 to +4 and +4 to +12 with other edge 3 ops (runs 6-8, 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with a 3x3 conv on edge 3 gave +3.8/+6.5/+17.5 (run 31), versus smaller gains when replacing skip, 1x1 or avg_pool (runs 32-34)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a skip on edge 3 with a 3x3 conv gained only +1/0/+3.7 (run 32), the smallest of the replacements tested (runs 31, 33, 34), because the skip already gives a cheap path."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Putting a pool on edge 1 cost -2/-5.3/-4.8 when edge 5 was already a pool (run 30), worse than with a conv on edge 5 (runs 28-29), because too many pooling edges lose capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a skip on edge 5 changed accuracy by +3.5/+3.5/+5.2 (run 81), whereas removing a 3x3 conv there